            <ArticleTitle>Alcohol, coronary heart disease, and total mortality.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>157-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The dose-response relationship between alcohol consumption, coronary heart disease, and total mortality was examined. The results indicated that moderate consumers (1 to 2 drinks/day) were at a lower risk of coronary heart disease than nonconsumers or heavy consumers. Evaluation of total mortality in relationship to alcohol consumption reveals that a similar U-shaped relationship to longevity exists.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
